# 06 §9 — adaptation
# RULE: power goes out at 3:00 every night, 11 minutes. Refrain: "Lights out, eyes in."
# COPING: 3 curtains per window (Pike's sells 900/yr) · bakery opens 3:11 · mayor's NOT LOOKING masks (wears 2)
# HERO: me, 10, now closes Bea's curtains (twice, like Dad). LOVED ONE: Bea, 6, leaves a cookie "for the one who turns the lights off".
# TABOO: looking outside. SEEDS: cookie gone (window locked) · fur high on the pole · 23 footprints, one per house ·
#        1994 newspaper "9 gone, all lights on" · it taps each window once per person (counting).
# ESCALATION: note "You looked." → lights out at 2:59 → knock on the roof → Bea turns her flashlight on.
# TWIST: "The giant was never hunting us. It was hiding us." That's why: lights out / checks windows / counts / cookies.
# PAYOFF: it takes Bea's cookie with 2 fingers, new note. STING (callback to the counting): 5 taps, "There are only 4 of us."
# v4 visual rule: every line shows what it says (CHEATSHEET §3.0).
title: The 3AM Neighbor
id: the-3am-neighbor
lang: en
voice: narrator_c2
home: wall=#9fc4e8 roof=#3f4a63 door=#c8323c trim=#ffffff
speak: 2:59=2 59

cast:
me    kid spiky #f2d232 | stripes_h #e7c43f #151515 | pants #151515
bea   kid ponytail #6b3f22 | pajamas_stars #7fb2ee #ffffff | bow
mom   adult bun #2a1d17 | cardigan #f0a6b8 #fff3f6 | pants #3b4a6b
dad   adult short #4a3426 | plaid #3a6ea5 #1d2b45 | pants #555555 | glasses
mayor adult short #2a2a2a | suit #1f2f5c #ffffff | pants #1f2f5c | tie mayor_chain mustache
beast creature furry_giant | scale 5

places:
my_room      bedroom variant=boy curtains=3
bea_room     bedroom variant=girl curtains=3
millers_room bedroom variant=parents curtains=3
mayor_room   bedroom variant=parents wall=#d8c8a4 curtains=3
kitchen      kitchen curtains=3
living_room  living_room curtains=3

== suburban_street night
In this town, the power goes out | est push
== card night
at 3:00 every night. | card:clock text=3:00 title=AM push
== suburban_street night dark
For exactly 11 minutes. | aer drift
== house_front night dark
Nobody looks outside. | est push
== my_room night
Lights out, eyes in. | wide me:pull_curtain>window opt:curtains.animate=close
That's the rule. | cu me:nod
== my_room day
Every window in town has 3 curtains. | ins s:window opt:curtains.animate=close push
== shop_front day sign=PIKE'S_HARDWARE display=curtains
Mr. Pike's hardware store | est push
sells 900 of them a year. | wide crowd:10:carry:smile>door
== card day
The bakery opens at 3:11. | card:sign_wood title="BAKERY" text="OPEN 3:11 AM" push
Never 3:00. | card:sign_wood title="BAKERY" text="CLOSED AT 3:00 AM" push
== town_square day
Our mayor gave every family | est mayor:offer@plaque crowd:14:stand>plaque
a sleep mask that says | mcu extra:smile:+sleep_mask2=NOT_LOOKING push
NOT LOOKING. | cu extra:smile:+sleep_mask=NOT_LOOKING push
He wears 2. | med mayor:wave:grin:+sleep_mask=NOT_LOOKING:+sleep_mask2=NOT_LOOKING push
== town_square dusk
Every night, the whole town says it. | est crowd:16:talk>statue
"Lights out, eyes in." | two extra:talk extra2:nod q:town
== kitchen night
Like goodnight. | wide mom:hug:smile me:smile
== bea_room night
My little sister Bea is 6. | wide bea:wave:grin
And she's not scared of anything. | cu bea:smirk push
Every night, she leaves a cookie | med bea:offer:smile:cookie>window
on her windowsill. | ins s:sill opt:sill=cookie push
"For the one who turns the lights off." | cu bea:talk:happy:cookie q:bea push
== living_room night
Dad checks every curtain twice. | wide dad:pull_curtain>window opt:curtains.animate=close
Once to close it. Once to be sure. | med dad:nod>window
== kitchen night dark
Mom hums the same song for 11 minutes. | med mom:sit_rock:happy@seat1 +candle@table
In the dark. | wide mom:sit_rock:happy@seat1 bea:sit:sleep@seat2 +candle@table
== my_room night
And this year, I'm 10. | med me:arms_up:grin
== bea_room night
So I close Bea's curtains now. | wide me:pull_curtain>window bea:lie:smile@bed opt:curtains.animate=close
Twice. Like Dad. | cu me:nod:smirk push
== my_room day
Then I started noticing things. | cu me:look_around:worried push
== bea_room day
Every morning, Bea's cookie was gone. | ins s:sill push
== kitchen day
Mom said birds. | med mom:shrug
== bea_room day
The window was locked. | med me:tap:worried>window
== suburban_street day
There was black fur on the power pole. | low s:pole_top +fur_tuft@pole_top tiltu
Way up. Higher than our roof. | wide me:point>pole_top >home_roof
In the mud, there were footprints | high s:footprint_trail +footprint_trail@road:count=6
as long as Dad's car. | med dad:surprised@driveway>road +giant_footprint@road
One in front of every house. | aer +footprint_trail@road:count=10:spacing=22 drift
== card day
23 houses. 23 footprints. | card:notebook title="MY NOTES" text="23 houses. 23 footprints." push
== library day
At the library, I found a newspaper from 1994. | est me:look_down:book@A push
== card day
9 people gone in one winter. | card:newspaper title="ELM DAILY - 1994" text="9 GONE IN ONE WINTER"
All from houses with the lights on. | card:newspaper title="ELM DAILY - 1994" text="All 9 houses had their lights on." push
== suburban_street night dark
The blackouts started the next year. | est drift
== bea_room night
Bea asked me who turns the lights off. | two bea:talk me:neutral
I said nobody. | med me:shrug
She said, "Then who eats the cookies?" | cu bea:talk:smirk:cookie q:bea push
== my_room night dark
So that night, at 3:00, | cu me:wide_eyes push
I opened my curtain. 1 inch. | ots me:peek >window opt:curtains.state=gap
== suburban_street night dark
Something was walking down our street. | est beast:walk@road^by_home pov:vignette
Taller than the power poles. | wide beast:walk@by_pole push
Black fur. | cu beast:walk@by_pole push
A grin as wide as a car. | xcu beast@by_pole push
It stopped at the Millers' house, | wide beast:bend@neighbor1
leaned down, and tapped their window. | med beast:tap@neighbor1 push
== millers_room night dark
Tap. Tap. Tap. | ins s:giant_hand +giant_hand@outside:pose=tap
3 Millers. | wide extra:scared extra2:scared extra3:scared
== mayor_room night dark
Then the mayor's house. Tap. | wide mayor:lie:sleep:+sleep_mask=NOT_LOOKING:+sleep_mask2=NOT_LOOKING@bed +giant_hand@outside:pose=tap
He lives alone. With his masks. | cu mayor:lie:sleep:+sleep_mask=NOT_LOOKING:+sleep_mask2=NOT_LOOKING@bed push
== suburban_street night dark
Then it stopped at our house. | wide beast:bend@by_home push
== my_room night dark
Tap. Tap. Tap. Tap. | ins s:giant_hand +giant_hand@outside:pose=tap
4. | cu me:wide_eyes push
== living_room night dark
Mom, Dad, Bea, me. | wide mom:scared dad:scared bea:sleep me:scared
== suburban_street night dark
It was counting us. | cu beast:tap@by_home push
== my_room night dark
Then it turned to my window. | ins s:window_face +window_face@outside
And it smiled. | xcu s:window_face +window_face@outside push
== house_front day
The next morning, | est push
there was a note on our door. | med me:surprised@porch>home_door +note_paper@home_door:text=You_looked.
== card day
"You looked." | card:note text="You looked." push
== kitchen day
Mom read it twice. | med mom:worried:note=You_looked.
== my_room day
Dad nailed my curtain shut. | med dad:hammer:hammer>window opt:boarded
"Lights out, eyes in," he said. | cu dad:angry q:dad push
== card night
The next night, the lights went out at 2:59. | card:clock text=2:59 title=AM push
== my_room night dark boarded
One minute early. | cu me:wide_eyes push
Then something knocked. | wide me:scared>door shake
Not on the door. | cu me:scared >door push
== rooftops_sky night dark
On the roof. | low beast:knock@over_home push
== bea_room night dark
Then I heard Bea's window open. | wide bea:reach>window opt:windowOpen
She had her flashlight. | mcu bea:carry:smile:flashlight
And a cookie. | cu bea:offer:happy:cookie push
Click. | ots bea:carry:flashlight=on >outside opt:windowOpen
== suburban_street night dark
The only light in the whole town. | est +candle@home_window:scale=3 push
At the end of the street, in the trees, | cam:to_forest push
something opened its eyes. | cu s:glowing_eyes +glowing_eyes@trees push
Lots of eyes. | wide s:glowing_eyes +glowing_eyes@trees:count=40
And they started coming toward the light. | med s:glowing_eyes +glowing_eyes@trees:approach=4 push
== bea_room night dark
I ran down the hall, into her room, | wide me:run:scared@D^A
and grabbed the flashlight. | mcu me:scared:flashlight=on
Click. Dark. | cu me:scared:flashlight push
== suburban_street night dark
But the eyes kept coming. | med s:glowing_eyes +glowing_eyes@trees:approach=6 push
Closer. | cu s:glowing_eyes +glowing_eyes@trees:approach=8 push
== house_front night dark
Then the ground shook. | est shake
== rooftops_sky night dark
Thud. | low beast:step@giant shake
== suburban_street night dark
Thud. | wide beast:walk@road^by_home shake
Thud. | cu beast:step@by_home shake
== rooftops_sky night dark
The giant stepped over our house | low beast:straddle@over_home push
== suburban_street night dark
and stood between us and the trees. | back beast:spread@guard>trees +glowing_eyes@trees
It spread its arms wide. | low beast:spread@guard push
The eyes stopped. | med s:glowing_eyes +glowing_eyes@trees
Then, one by one, they closed. | med s:glowing_eyes +glowing_eyes@trees:close=true
== rooftops_sky night dark
The giant was never hunting us. | low beast:spread@over_home push
It was hiding us. | high beast:straddle@over_home
== suburban_street night dark
That's why the lights go out at 3:00. | aer drift
The things in the trees can only find us by our light. | wide s:glowing_eyes +glowing_eyes@trees >home
That's why it checks every window. | wide beast:tap@neighbor2
== bea_room night dark
One light is enough. | ots bea:carry:flashlight=on >outside
== suburban_street night dark
That's why it counts us, every house, every night. | wide beast:tap@neighbor1
== town_square day
Nobody's gone missing since 1994. | est crowd:18:happy>statue
== bea_room night dark
And that's why the cookies were gone. | ins s:sill opt:sill=cookie +giant_hand@outside:pose=open
Bea held out her cookie. | med bea:offer:happy:cookie>window opt:windowOpen
== suburban_street night dark
The giant bent down, all the way down, | wide beast:bend@by_home push
== bea_room night dark
and took it with 2 fingers. | ins s:giant_hand +giant_hand@outside:pose=pinch:holding=cookie opt:windowOpen
Very, very carefully. | mcu bea:happy +giant_hand@outside:pose=pinch:holding=cookie opt:windowOpen
Then it tapped her window. Once. | ins s:giant_hand +giant_hand@outside:pose=tap
Bea tapped back. | ots bea:tap >window +giant_hand@outside:pose=open
== house_front day
The next morning, there was a new note. | med me:smile@porch>home_door +note_paper@home_door:text=Thank_you_for_the_cookie.
== card day
"Thank you for the cookie." | card:note text="Thank you for the cookie." push
"Lights out, eyes in." | card:note text="Thank you for the cookie. Lights out, eyes in." push
== card night
Last night, the power went out at 3:00. | card:clock text=3:00 title=AM push
== suburban_street night dark
Like always. | est drift
The giant walked down our street, | wide beast:walk@road^by_home
checking every house. | wide beast:bend@neighbor2
It stopped at ours. | wide beast:bend@by_home push
== my_room night dark
Tap. Tap. Tap. Tap. Tap. | ins s:giant_hand +giant_hand@outside:pose=tap
There are only 4 of us. | cu me:wide_eyes push
